        "id": "s1",
        "title": {
          "en": "The third night",
          "hi": "तीसरी रात"
        },
        "image": {
          "id": "future-sya-s1",
          "brief": "The burning-ground grove at night: a slim spirit of pale morning light leaning forward as if about to run, hair streaming ahead; the Vetāla hanging above with a sly look; you, Dādī and Śuka in the foreground; a glow of dawn beginning at the far edge of the trees.",
          "alt": {
            "en": "A pale spirit leans forward as if about to run while the Vetāla hangs above with a sly look",
            "hi": "पीला भूत दौड़ने को आगे झुकता, ऊपर चालाक मुद्रा में वेताल"
          },
          "text_in_image": [],
          "ratio": "4:3",
          "cast": [
            "you",
            "dadi",
            "shuka",
            "vetala",
            "bhavika"
          ],
          "place": "smashana"
        },
        "depth": "core",
        "skills": [],
        "sutras": [],
        "kind": "story",
        "narration": {
          "en": "“Tell me,” the Vetāla asks lazily, “what will you do if the collector finds the leaves?” You open your mouth and know only “I read” and “I read yesterday”. A slim spirit of pale light leans in from the dark, as if about to run. “गमिष्यति,” he says, eager. “पठिष्यति.” “He will go, he will read,” Dādī says. “The sign is -ष्य-.”",
          "hi": "“बताओ,” वेताल सुस्ती से पूछता है, “अगर संग्रहकर्ता को पत्र मिल गए तो तुम क्या करोगे?” आप मुँह खोलते हैं और जानते हैं केवल ‘मैं पढ़ता हूँ’ और ‘मैंने कल पढ़ा’। पीला प्रकाश-सा एक पतला भूत अँधेरे से आगे झुकता है, मानो अभी दौड़ पड़ेगा। “गमिष्यति,” वह उत्सुकता से कहता है। “पठिष्यति।” “वह जाएगा, वह पढ़ेगा,” दादी कहती हैं। “इसका चिह्न -ष्य- है।”"
        },
        "lines": [
